.SH NAME
ionxnowner \- report on which threads are initiating SDR transactions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBionxnowner\fR [\fIinterval\fR [\fIcount\fR [\fIecho\fR]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
For \fIcount\fR interations (defaulting to 1), \fBionxnowner\fR prints the
process ID and thread ID of the thread that currently "owns" the 
local node's SDR data store (i.e., started the current transaction), then
sleeps \fIinterval\fR seconds (minimum 1).  If the optional \fIecho\fR parameter
is set to 1, then the transaction owner message is logged as well as
printed to the console.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
\&\fBionxnowner\fR has terminated.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
No configuration files are needed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
